│ The issue describes a problem where          │
│ FileInput incorrectly displays a “required”  │
│ attribute when a file has already been set.  │
│ This happens because ClearableFileInput’s    │
│ use_required_attribute() method is being     │
│ called, and it’s adding the required         │
│ attribute to the HTML input element even     │
│ when the file is already associated with the │
│ form. The fix is to move the                 │
│ use_required_attribute() call from           │
│ ClearableFileInput to FileInput itself. This │
│ ensures that the required attribute is only  │
│ added when a file is not already associated  │
│ with the form.                               │
